+## TL;DR
+- `OCRmyPDF`, `docTR`, `Tesseract`, `MarkItDown`, and `Unstructured` are the strongest open source starting points for policy PDFs, ACORD forms, and claims paperwork.
+- `RAGFlow`, `Haystack`, `AnythingLLM`, `Kotaemon`, and `Agentset` are the best fits for internal knowledge assistants over underwriting guides, product manuals, and SOPs.
+- `LiveKit Agents`, `Pipecat`, `Vocode`, `Intervo`, and `Rhasspy` cover voice-first workflows such as inbound call triage, renewal reminders, and self-service policy questions.
+- `n8n`, `Activepieces`, `Dify`, `Flowise`, and `Langflow` help agencies automate lead routing, document enrichment, follow-up sequences, and agent handoffs.
+- `Ollama`, `LocalAI`, `vLLM`, `Qdrant`, and `pgvector` are the core building blocks for private, self-hosted insurance AI stacks.
+
+## Why This List
+The best AI tools for insurance agents are usually not labeled "for insurance" on GitHub. Most agencies need a stack that combines document extraction, retrieval, workflow automation, voice handling, and private model serving rather than a single vertical app. This list therefore focuses on open source repositories that map well to real insurance agency work while remaining auditable, forkable, and deployable without proprietary SaaS lock-in.
+
+Insurance-specific gaps are real and worth documenting honestly:
+- Pure-play open source agency management systems with modern AI features had fewer than 5 suitable public GitHub repos.
+- Open source carrier quoting copilots and underwriting assistants had fewer than 5 suitable public GitHub repos.
+- Open source claims-only AI tools aimed specifically at retail insurance agents had fewer than 5 suitable public GitHub repos.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Document Intake, OCR, and Extraction
+
+#### [OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/ocrmypdf/OCRmyPDF)
+> **Description:** OCRmyPDF adds an OCR text layer to scanned PDFs while preserving the original document, making it useful for policy packets, applications, endorsements, and scanned claims files. The project README emphasizes searchable PDF generation, image cleanup, deskewing, PDF/A output, and automation-friendly command-line usage. Its open source license and mature CLI make it practical for back-office ingestion pipelines where insurance teams need searchable records without sending files to a third-party SaaS.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/ocrmypdf/OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/ocrmypdf/OCRmyPDF)
+- **Stars:** 33k ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** MPL-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** 2026-03
+- **Category:** OCR, PDF, document-processing
+- **Best for:** Turning scanned policy and claims PDFs into searchable files
+
+---
+
+#### [docTR](https://github.com/mindee/doctr)
+> **Description:** docTR is an end-to-end document text detection and OCR toolkit built for structured documents. Its README highlights deep-learning based detection and recognition, support for TensorFlow and PyTorch, and utilities for extracting words, lines, and pages from business documents. For insurance operations, it is a strong fit when teams need more programmable OCR than a desktop scanner workflow and want to build custom extraction pipelines for applications, ACORD forms, invoices, or loss runs using an Apache-licensed codebase.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/mindee/doctr](https://github.com/mindee/doctr)
+- **Stars:** 6k ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** 2026-03
+- **Category:** OCR, deep-learning, forms
+- **Best for:** Custom extraction flows for forms and semi-structured insurance documents
+
+---
+
+#### [Tesseract OCR](https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract)
+> **Description:** Tesseract is the long-running open source OCR engine used across many document workflows. The README positions it as a powerful OCR engine with LSTM-based recognition, multiple language packs, and integrations across operating systems and programming environments. Insurance agencies often use it as the lowest-level OCR building block in larger ingestion pipelines, especially when they need a stable, widely adopted engine that can be embedded inside self-hosted systems for compliance-sensitive records and scanned correspondence.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract](https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract)
+- **Stars:** 71.8k ⭐
+- **Language:** C++
