+- **Stars:** 93k ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** MIT
+- **Last Commit:** 2026-03
+- **Category:** document-conversion, markdown, preprocessing
+- **Best for:** Converting office docs and attachments into LLM-ready text
+
+---
+
+#### [Unstructured](https://github.com/unstructured-io/unstructured)
+> **Description:** Unstructured is a document ingestion and preprocessing library designed to convert raw enterprise files into structured elements for NLP and LLM use. Its README focuses on connectors, partitioning, chunking, document element extraction, and support for many file types. In an insurance setting, that matters because agencies often need a repeatable way to ingest PDFs, DOCX files, emails, HTML portals, and spreadsheets before building quote copilots or internal search over underwriting and service documentation.
